BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsasquatchhuntadult26familyexpeditions23838-20261118@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261115T165621Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:Sasquatch Hunt - Adult & Family Expeditions
DESCRIPTION:Truth-seekers\, MythBusters\, and folklorists—unite! Reports have surfaced that the elusive Bigfoot —yes\, the legend himself—has wandered far from the misty forests of the Pacific Northwest and taken up winter residence right here in Frederick County. His chosen hideout? The shadowy trails of Othello Park. Frederick County Parks and Recreation is calling on fun-loving adventurers - both solo explorers and fun-loving groups - to join an exclusive expedition to uncover clues\, undeniable evidence\, and perhaps—just perhaps—be the ones to finally solve this legendary mystery. Each discovery earns you raffle tickets for a chance to win amazing prizes from local businesses. Whether you're a devoted believer or a curious skeptic\, this is one adventure you won’t want to miss! So\, lace up your boots\, sharpen your senses\, and prepare for a legendary park adventure. Who knows what—or who—you’ll find out there (1) registration is good for up to 5 household (share the same residence) family members. Family Expedition: This 1-mile loop features moderate terrain\, with mostly even footing and slight elevation changes. This event is open to all ages and involves walking\, so we encourage families to participate at a pace that feels comfortable for them within the allotted time. Trail map provided\; map does not include locations of clues. Event held rain or shine. Additional information to follow in email the week of the event. This session will be held during daylight hours.... perfect for those who feel more comfortable participating before it gets dark! At 6:30 PM the Adult Sasquatch Hunt will begin. The trail spans approximately 2 miles\, featuring moderate terrain with generally even footing and gentle inclines and declines. Trail map provided\; map does not include locations of clues. Please bring headlamp and/or standard flashlight. Event held rain or shine. Additional information to follow in email the week of the event. (1) Registration covers a duo team—or a solo adventurer\, if you dare!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/sasquatch-hunt-adult-%26-family-expeditions/23838/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsongwritersworkshop26209-20261118@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261115T165621Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:Songwriter's Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Are you a musician looking for inspiration/feedback? Or\, maybe you’d just like the chance to perform your newest song! Oh boy\, have we got the event for you. Join us for another one of our free songwriting workshops presented by Braindead Live! with the opportunity to perform your song(s)! Workshop signups at 6:45PM. BYO instrument(s) and creativity! PS. Even if you are not interested in participating in the workshop\, this will be a fun\, free event where you\, as an audience member\, will have the opportunity to watch a musician’s creative journey from inception to performance!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/songwriters-workshop/26209/
END:VEVENT
